---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/site';
const guides = [
  { path: '/guides/sba-charge-off-rate/', title: 'What an SBA charge-off rate is', blurb: 'What a charge-off means, how it differs from "failure", and why seasoned cohorts matter.' },
  { path: '/guides/franchise-disclosure-item-19-20/', title: 'Reading Item 19 and Item 20 next to SBA loan records', blurb: 'How franchisor disclosures and public loan outcomes complement each other, and what to ask.' },
  { path: '/guides/compare-two-franchise-brands/', title: 'Comparing two franchise brands', blurb: 'A short routine for fair comparisons: same cohort, sample sizes, confidence intervals.' },
];
---
<Base title="Guides: reading SBA franchise loan records" description="Plain-language guides to reading SBA 7(a) charge-off records for franchise brands: what a charge-off rate means, how to use Item 19 and Item 20, and how to compare two brands fairly." crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides' }]}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Guides</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short explanations of how to read the SBA loan records on this site, written for people weighing a franchise purchase. They explain method and limits; every figure on the site comes from the published data.</p>
    <ul>
      {guides.map((g) => (
        <li><a href={url(g.path)}>{g.title}</a>. {g.blurb}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>To see the records themselves, start with the <a href={url('/rankings/')}>rankings</a>, the <a href={url('/compare/')}>compare tool</a> or the <a href={url('/methodology/')}>methodology</a>. This site is independent and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the SBA, and nothing here is financial or legal advice.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
